# Juno - AI Computer Use Agent Project Overview

## Project Description
Juno is a Tauri v2 application featuring an advanced AI Computer Use Bot with Anthropic capabilities. The application combines a React/TypeScript frontend with a Rust backend to provide desktop automation and AI-powered computer interaction.

## Key Architecture Components

### Frontend (React/TypeScript)
- Modern React application with TypeScript
- Tauri v2 integration for native desktop capabilities
- Voice control interface
- Real-time communication with Rust backend

### Backend (Rust)
- **Main Application**: [src-tauri/src/lib.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/lib.rs) - Core Tauri app setup and initialization
- **Voice Control**: [src-tauri/src/voice_control.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/voice_control.rs) - Whisper-based speech recognition
- **Agent System**: [src-tauri/src/agent/](mdc:src-tauri/src/agent/) - AI agent implementations and tools
- **MCP Server**: [src-tauri/mcp-server-os-level/](mdc:src-tauri/mcp-server-os-level/) - Model Context Protocol server for OS-level automation

### AI Providers
- **Anthropic**: [src-tauri/src/agent/providers/anthropic.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/agent/providers/anthropic.rs) - Claude integration
- **Rig Framework**: [src-tauri/src/agent/providers/rig.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/agent/providers/rig.rs) - Multi-model AI provider support
- **OpenAI**: Integrated through Rig framework

### Desktop Automation
- **macOS Engine**: [src-tauri/mcp-server-os-level/src/platforms/macos/engine.rs](mdc:src-tauri/mcp-server-os-level/src/platforms/macos/engine.rs) - Accessibility API integration
- **Browser Tools**: [src-tauri/src/agent/tools/browser_tools.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/agent/tools/browser_tools.rs) - Web automation capabilities
- **Basic Tools**: [src-tauri/src/agent/tools/basic_tools.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/agent/tools/basic_tools.rs) - File system and command execution

## Development Tools
- **Package Manager**: Bun (primary), with npm/yarn as fallbacks
- **Build System**: Tauri CLI v2
- **Language**: Rust (backend), TypeScript/React (frontend)
- **Testing**: Custom QA commands for automation testing

## Key Features
- Real-time voice dictation and transcription
- Desktop automation (mouse, keyboard, window management)
- Multi-modal AI agent with tool execution
- Browser automation capabilities
- Cross-platform desktop application (macOS focused)
- TTS (Text-to-Speech) integration
- Screenshot and visual element detection

## Production Considerations
- Environment variables for API keys (see [.env.example](mdc:.env.example))
- Security sandboxing for file operations (TODO items noted)
- Accessibility permissions required for desktop automation
- Model files for local Whisper inference

## Getting Started
1. Install dependencies: `bun install`
2. Set up environment variables from `.env.example`
3. Build and run: `bun tauri dev`
4. For production: `bun tauri build`
